From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: serlk <22211586+Serlk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 04:02:25 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 17/21] clk: mediatek: mt6878-cam: Keep the camsys providers
 active through system sleep

At every system resume the CAM_MAIN power domain failed to come back
("cam-main: power on failed: -13"): genpd powers the camera SMI domain
back on in resume_noirq, SCPSYS prepares the domain's camsys clocks, and
the clock framework resumes their provider device through runtime PM,
which refuses a device that is not active between the late suspend and
the early resume. The provider devices power and clock nothing through
their runtime state, so .prepare now takes a runtime PM reference while
runtime PM still works and .complete drops it again.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6878-cam.c | 45 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 45 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6878-cam.c b/drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6878-cam.c
index 6640a624d5f5..d1051c704ce2 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6878-cam.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6878-cam.c
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/of_device.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
+#include <linux/pm_runtime.h>
 
 #include "clk-gate.h"
 #include "clk-mtk.h"
@@ -304,12 +305,56 @@ static const struct of_device_id of_match_clk_mt6878_cam[] = {
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, of_match_clk_mt6878_cam);
 
+/*
+ * The camsys gates are clocks of the CAM power domains (cam-main, cam-suba,
+ * cam-subb, cam-vcore, ...), which the SCPSYS power domain driver prepares
+ * and enables when it switches such a domain on, also in the noirq phase of
+ * a system resume (genpd powers the domain of a device back on there).
+ * Preparing a clock resumes its provider device through runtime PM, which
+ * is disabled from the late suspend to the early resume phase and then
+ * refuses (-EACCES) a device whose state and saved state are not both
+ * active: "cam-main: power on failed: -13".
+ *
+ * The provider devices have no power domain of their own and no runtime
+ * PM callbacks: an active runtime state powers or clocks nothing. So take
+ * a runtime PM reference on each in .prepare, while runtime PM still works,
+ * and drop it in .complete, which also runs for an aborted sleep. Their
+ * runtime state is then active, and saved as active, through the late and
+ * noirq phases. The CAM domains are not touched by this; they stay under
+ * SCPSYS, the gates under the clock framework.
+ */
+static int clk_mt6878_cam_pm_prepare(struct device *dev)
+{
+	int ret = pm_runtime_get_sync(dev);
+
+	if (ret < 0)
+		dev_warn(dev, "not held active for the system sleep: %d\n", ret);
+	else
+		dev_dbg(dev, "held active for the system sleep (usage %d)\n",
+			atomic_read(&dev->power.usage_count));
+	/* the reference is dropped in .complete either way */
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static void clk_mt6878_cam_pm_complete(struct device *dev)
+{
+	pm_runtime_put(dev);
+	dev_dbg(dev, "released after the system sleep (usage %d)\n",
+		atomic_read(&dev->power.usage_count));
+}
+
+static const struct dev_pm_ops clk_mt6878_cam_pm_ops = {
+	.prepare = clk_mt6878_cam_pm_prepare,
+	.complete = clk_mt6878_cam_pm_complete,
+};
+
 static struct platform_driver clk_mt6878_cam_drv = {
 	.probe = mtk_clk_simple_probe,
 	.remove = mtk_clk_simple_remove,
 	.driver = {
 		.name = "clk-mt6878-cam",
 		.of_match_table = of_match_clk_mt6878_cam,
+		.pm = pm_sleep_ptr(&clk_mt6878_cam_pm_ops),
 	},
 };
 module_platform_driver(clk_mt6878_cam_drv);
-- 
